From: Johan Alvarado <contact@c127.dev>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 00:20:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: disable irqs before freeing rings on crash
 recovery

ath11k_core_reconfigure_on_crash() frees the data path rings and clears
the srngs, then calls ath11k_core_qmi_firmware_ready(), which re-enables
the copy engine interrupts through ath11k_hif_start(). Nothing in this
path ever disables those interrupts: the crash path does not run
ath11k_core_stop(), which is the only caller of ath11k_hif_stop().

So the interrupts stay live across the teardown. On IPQ5018 with a
QCN6122, which uses the pcic irq ops, re-enabling them delivers a CE
interrupt inside ath11k_pcic_ce_irqs_enable() itself, the NAPI poll runs
against an srng that ath11k_hal_srng_clear() has already cleared, and the
NULL dereference is fatal because it happens in interrupt context:

  Unbalanced enable for IRQ 64
  WARNING: CPU: 0 PID: 12 at kernel/irq/manage.c:774 __enable_irq+0x4c/0x7c
  ...
  Unable to handle kernel read from unreadable memory at virtual address 0
  pc : ath11k_hal_srng_access_begin+0xc/0x60 [ath11k]
  lr : ath11k_dp_rx_process_mon_status+0x150/0xe04 [ath11k]
  Call trace:
   ath11k_dp_rx_process_mon_rings+0x8c/0x5ec [ath11k]
   ath11k_dp_service_srng+0x1f4/0x358 [ath11k]
   ath11k_ahb_ext_grp_napi_poll+0x34/0xc8 [ath11k_ahb]
   ...
   ath11k_pcic_ce_irqs_enable+0x78/0x9c [ath11k]
   ath11k_pcic_start+0x34/0x5c [ath11k]
   ath11k_core_qmi_firmware_ready+0x104/0x584 [ath11k]
   ath11k_core_restart+0xb4/0x144 [ath11k]
  Kernel panic - not syncing: Oops: Fatal exception in interrupt

This only became reachable once subsystem restart started working on
IPQ5018; before that the Q6 never came back, so the recovery path was
never exercised.

Disable the ext and CE interrupts, and with them NAPI, before the rings
are torn down. That also removes the unbalanced enable, since the crash
path now has the disable that matches the enable in ath11k_hif_start().

Signed-off-by: Johan Alvarado <contact@c127.dev>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
@@ -2365,6 +2365,27 @@
 {
 	int ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * The firmware is gone, but the data path interrupts are still live:
+	 * this path never runs ath11k_core_stop(), so nothing has disabled
+	 * them. Shut the ext interrupts and NAPI down before the rings are
+	 * freed below, otherwise a DP interrupt taken while
+	 * ath11k_core_qmi_firmware_ready() re-enables the copy engine runs the
+	 * NAPI poll against an srng that ath11k_hal_srng_clear() has already
+	 * cleared, and the NULL dereference is fatal in interrupt context:
+	 *
+	 *   pc : ath11k_hal_srng_access_begin+0xc/0x60 [ath11k]
+	 *   lr : ath11k_dp_rx_process_mon_status+0x150/0xe04 [ath11k]
+	 *   Kernel panic - not syncing: Oops: Fatal exception in interrupt
+	 *
+	 * Only on a real crash: this function also runs for the cold boot
+	 * calibration restart, where the interrupts were never enabled, and
+	 * disabling them there leaves them disabled through the following
+	 * enable, so the radio never takes another interrupt.
+	 */
+	if (test_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_RECOVERY, &ab->dev_flags))
+		ath11k_hif_irq_disable(ab);
+
 	mutex_lock(&ab->core_lock);
 	ath11k_thermal_unregister(ab);
 	ath11k_dp_pdev_free(ab);
